# Story 66: Project Notes (40s)
# Hook: A shared scratchpad your agent reads and writes for the whole project.
# Duration: 40s
# Source: story-066-project-notes.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 5

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
A shared scratchpad your agent reads and writes for the whole project.

[00:03.0 --> 00:08.0]
Start rysh and drop into prompt mode.

[00:08.0 --> 00:22.0]
Ask the agent to note a project decision. The project_notes tool appends it to a shared .rysh-notes.md file.

[00:22.0 --> 00:32.0]
Back in shell mode, the notes live in a plain markdown file you can open, edit, and commit alongside your code.

[00:32.0 --> 00:40.0]
project_notes is durable, file-backed memory that every pane and every agent on the project can share.

